Description: Unofficial Wine wrapper for the Fork git client
 Fork for Linux (unofficial) runs the official, unmodified Fork for Windows
 git client under Wine, with a menu entry, a "fork" command for opening
 repositories, update snapshots with rollback and a health check.
 .
 Fork is proprietary, paid software made by Dan Pristupov and Tanya
 Pristupova (https://git-fork.com). The evaluation is free; please buy a
 license at https://git-fork.com/buy if you keep using it.
 .
 This package is not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by the Fork
 developers. It contains only the wrapper: at first run it downloads a
 pinned Wine runtime, Microsoft .NET Framework (under Microsoft's terms) and
 the official Fork installer from cdn.fork.dev into the user's home
 directory, and it never redistributes, patches or decompiles Fork. It does
 not use the distribution's wine package and never touches ~/.wine.
 Report wrapper problems at https://github.com/ventura8/Fork-Linux/issues.
